To divide by a fraction, multiply by its reciprocal:
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{4x^2}{3y} \div \frac{xy}{5} &= \frac{4x^2}{3y} \times \frac{5}{xy} \\
&= \frac{4x^2 \times 5}{3y \times xy} \\
&= \frac{20x^2}{3xy^2}
\end{align*}$$
Cancel the common factor of $x$ from the numerator and denominator:
$$\begin{align*}
&= \frac{20x}{3y^2}
\end{align*}$$
